PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Round 1 shows strong convergence on Donizetti's La Favorita (Leonora title role): Alboni confirmed in 1843 La Scala revival (multiple cols), Caruso as Fernando in 1905 Met run, first post-Caruso NYC staging in 1975/78 Met revival (or close OONY variant) satisfying >70yr gap exactly. Bass Baldassare = Bonaldo Giaiotti per 10,11,12,15,18,19,20,3,4,6,8,1 (PUBLIC RESPONSE citations). 

Dissenting minority (13,14,16,17,2,5,7,9,21) still cite Ezio Pinza (1940s Met timeline, Don Giovanni resonance, or 1905 gap miscalc) at 30-40% confidence, often conflating operas or questioning Giaiotti program notes as "Scala bleed-in." These fail the Alboni/1843 title-role + strict Met-then-NYC phrasing constraints.

Prior round candidates (Cenerentola/Alaimo/Ramey, La Juive/Ramey, Tancredi/Ramey, Saffo) rejected by majority for timeline/role mismatches. Unresolved: exact 1843 cast verification + whether 1975/78 or 2005 is the "first" staging meant. Favorita/Giaiotti now has clearest internal consistency; my belief strengthened. Need to cross-check any remaining Pinza/Don Giovanni program fragments next.}

